\begin_layout Abstract
Machine learning methods, in particular reinforcement learning, enable the
 learning of policies for technical systems.
 In order to increase the acceptance for solutions, it is advantageous that
 the solution resembles previously known solutions.
 As a solution, it is proposed to calculate the familiarity on the basis
 of the necessary edits to an expert program and to use it as a complexity
 measure for genetic programming.
 The approach was tested on the Mountain car and the Industrial Benchmark
 in the form of a symbolic regression of the transition samples of a neuropolicy.
 As a direct extension to the edit-distance, the specification of a fixed
 core structure was also implemented and tested.
 The candidates of familial GP approaches differ significantly from normal
 GP solutions.
 Familiar elements are clearly recognizable and the performance comparably
 good, sometimes better.
 The fixed core structure additionally enabled the preservation of familiar
 structures in very small programs, but also accelerated runs with complex
 programs (with more than 25 start nodes).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Abstract
The experiments conducted showed that the candidates found were more familiar,
 with comparable or better performance.
 Also extension possibilities like the definition of a program framework
 by the expert produce very promising results.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Note Note
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Explainability is hard to achieve in the field of RL, where the great successes
 relies on black box approaches like neural networks.
 In many domains in industry and science, Genetic programming (GP) offers
 the opportunity to automatically generate programs that are interpretable,
 but often represent mathematic expressions which are still hard to fully
 understand completely.
 For a domain expert, it would be very helpful to be shown where his own
 strategy could be improved.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Lösungen mit GP ohne Vorgaben sind oft naja.
 wir versuchen deshalb, GP zu nutzen um Lösungen zu finden, die bekannte
 Lösungsstrategien mit möglichst geringfügigen Änderungen verbessern können.
 Therefore, the concept of familiarity is introduced as quality criterion
 for GP, which measures the deviation from an expert's original program
 instead of pure complexity.
 This is realised with the tree edit distance as measure, which reflects
 the number of changes to the reference program.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The approach was testet on the mountaincar and the industrial benchmark,
 with several different neuropolicies provdiding transition samples als
 Basis für den Regressionsfehler.
 The results have shown no major drawbacks in terms of regression error
 and fitness, while staying closer to the domain experts approach.
 The real fitness evaluation seems to have a slight tendency for more stable
 results, but seem to depend rather on the volatility of the black box and
 how good the result could be achieved.
\end_layout

