\begin_layout Standard
The interpretability gap represents the learning effort, which an individual
 has to make to understand a black box.
 For optimal interpretability of policies, they should be as close as possible
 to the expert policy while having the performance of the black box.
 To close this gap between the expert's approach and a black box, we want
 to automatically produce similar programs that improve to be as good as
 the black box agent.
