\begin_layout Paragraph
Technical Realisation
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Fitness evaluation is the bottleneck of performance.
 Kai Staats has shown with KarooGP that a 2-15 times speedup can be achieved
 by converting expressions into Tensorflow graphs, which enables parallel
 evaluation on the GPU.
 To further enable simplification of expressions, the Python library SymPy
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "10.7717/peerj-cs.103"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 was extended and integrated, which uses symbolic mathematics and thus sifts
 out unnecessary calculations before evaluation.
 [xx see sympy errors] The memory usage and performance could be further
 increased, largely thanks to the help of lookup-tables for tree evaluation,
 passing variables locally and especially using recursive tree structures.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
No reliable statistics on the running time were compiled, but the running
 time was about only 50% in all comparison runs and the memory could be
 reduced to almost 10% of Karoo GP.
 xxx
\end_layout

\end_inset


