\begin_layout Standard
Fixed nodes were implemented in addition to the TED, which has shown in
 a very early stage to loose its protective effect for very small trees.
 Therefore, the expert has the chance to manually select nodes that should
 not be affected by the GP process in his origin tree.
 By explicitly securing the core structure, the GP process binds more [xxx
 rewrite] closely to the preferences of the developer.
 Especially when the developer is sure of the correctness of his abstraction,
 pointless optimization attempts of the GP process can be prevented.
 This reduces the run time and the search space.
 For very large trees, fixed nodes are actually mandatory to have the search
 space reduced.
\end_layout

