\begin_inset Caption Standard

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Overview of the most important IB features.
 The reward can not be used in the GP-process.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The Industrial Benchmark was introduced by scientists at Siemens to meet
 the high requirements of complex, real world industrial processes.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "industrialBenchmark"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 The state space is high-dimensional and only partially observable (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "IB-observations-state"

\end_inset

) and the reward depends on a combination of actions 0 and 1, as well as
 action 2, which severely penalizes misconduct.
 The development of observations have to be taken into account (in the form
 of retrospective consideration).
 Finally, high stochastic system dynamics further complicates learning reliable
 policies.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
No good human-developed control strategies for the IB are known; the best
 available strategy is doing 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

nothing
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

, which is also considered to be respectably good.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Black box
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As black box, 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout


\backslash
emph{particle swarm optimisation neural networks} (PSONN)
\end_layout

\end_inset

 with a calculated IB reward of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

 was chosen 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "PSONN_fuzzy_RL_Hein_Udluft"
literal "true"

\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The initial states of the IB in 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "daniel_hein_doktorarbeit"
literal "true"

\end_inset

 were randomized.
 Comparable values could be obtained by a randomized initial state, but
 the results were very volatile.
 The difference of agents in Hein's work was 7% worse on average.
 This value was used for comparison.
 For the PSONN policy, this results in a adjusted penalty value of 
\begin_inset ERT
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout

$5728/1.07=5353$
\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\end_layout

\end_inset

 Particle swarm optimisation algorithms, similar to GP, can find solutions
 for many types of problems.
 The solution space is populated by a swarm population, which should find
 the best optima by swarm intelligence.
 This approach is very interesting as a black box, because the model is
 very sparse and might be difficult to fit with symbolic regression.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Offline Data Selection
\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:Offline-Data-Selection"

\end_inset

 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The data for the symbolic regression are generated online, on the benchmark,
 from the chosen black box approach.
 All observable states and the associated actions are saved (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "data-collection-for-benchmarks"

\end_inset

).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the priority is to improve performance, data selection is conceivable,
 but stochasticity or long-term strategies are often hard to distinguish
 from actual misconduct.
 Clustering for yet unknown state-combinations in the black box data compared,
 compared to the current solution was also discarded to guarantee balanced
 and authentic results.
\end_layout

