\begin_layout Chapter
Results
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In this section, a large number of familiarity-based GP runs are evaluated
 and compared with regular GP runs, six of these are presented in more detail.
 The Pareto candidates found are primarily examined for familiarity and
 interpretability.
 Their performance is compared both in terms of regression error and real
 fitness, but also examined for implications for security.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
All runs were performed with both MAE and MSE, MSE runs were comparatively
 often better on the real benchmarks.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Section
Mountain car
\end_layout

\begin_layout Paragraph
Domain Expert solutions
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following, three solution strategies are examined more closely by
 experts as origin.
 A simple one, which relies on maximum acceleration and two extensive ones
 that feature complex strategies.
 One of them is a formula based on parabolas, the other is an extremely
 improved, nested if-statement that treats the reversal points as special
 cases.
 At sensible points, the options of fixed core structure and obligatory
 acceleration were tested.
 Since action 1 cannot be selected for the latter option, the regression
 error cannot drop to 0 (0.023 for SARSA-200, 0.066 for SARSA-75).
 
\end_layout

