\begin_layout Standard
The regular GP runs could completely solve the problem from complexity 18.
 Altering approaches are noticeable in the medium-complex candidate range
 (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:mtc200-mse-scratch-pareto"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

).
 Candidates do not try to distinguish between action 0 and 1, but provide
 a continuous and often fluctuating mathematical mapping between inputs
 and outputs (
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand formatted
reference "fig:MC-scratch-3examples"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

).
 Simple agents show a poor performance on the real benchmark and could not
 exceed the maximum-momentum strategy.
 
\end_layout

